    basic: "Once partner is known, direct trick points to your side; play high-value cards (A, 10, K) to partner's tricks (smearing). Lead fail aces early to win 11 points or draw trumps.",
    intermediate: 'If holding Spade Q, leading a high trump can invite partner to reveal with Club Q. Hold the Diamond 7 (Spitzer) to beat Spade Q when opportune; track which fail suits have been played.',
    advanced: 'Double-cutting a led fail ace (trumping then being overtrumped) is a key tactic. After a fail suit has been played twice, leading it again is effectively leading trump. Distribute smear cards early; later in the hand you have less control.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'The Diamond 7 (Spitzer) is the only card that beats the Spade Q (Little Queen) besides the Club Q.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Keep track of fail suits played; a suit cannot go around twice without being trumped.',
      },
